# Tasks

Copy this file to `tasks.md` in your project root and fill it in. The `django-task-runner`
subagent reads it on every iteration of `just task-run`, picks the first `**Status**: pending`
entry, implements it, marks it `done`, and writes a note under `progress/`.

The script counts `**Status**: pending` lines and stops when none remain or after
3 iterations without progress.

---

## T001 — Short title for the task

**Status**: pending

**Description**: Self-contained, one-paragraph statement of what needs to be done.
Assume the agent has no memory of prior conversations. Be specific about the *what*,
not the *how* — the agent decides the implementation.

**Context**: Point at concrete files and patterns. Examples:
- "Mirror the structure of `users/views.py` and `users/serializers.py`."
- "The new model lives in a new app `applications/`. Create it with `python manage.py startapp applications`."
- "The endpoint must use the `BaseModelViewSet` permissions/serializers dicts pattern (see docs/conventions.md)."

If this task depends on a previous one, say so: "T002 created the `Applicant` model; reuse it here."

**Acceptance criteria**:
- [ ] Endpoint `POST /api/applications/` exists and returns 201 with `{ id, name }` for valid input.
- [ ] Anonymous requests get 401.
- [ ] Invalid payload returns 400 with field errors.
- [ ] Migration generated and runs clean (`just migrate`).
- [ ] Tests in `applications/tests.py` cover the three cases above.
- [ ] `just lint`, `just test`, `just schema-validate` all pass.

